A bibliography and an index, compiled by the engine host with no TeX Live
(scripts/notex-host-check.sh, notex-gate.yml): with external tools allowed the
host runs its own bibtex and makeindex (lane RUST-TOOLS), and their outputs
must equal expected/, which TeX Live 2026's bibtex and makeindex made from the
same files as latexmk runs them (`pdflatex main`, `bibtex main`,
`makeindex -o main.ind main.idx`).

plain.bst is TeX Live 2026's, unmodified (its terms allow unmodified copies).
It is here because the published bundle (texbundle-tl2026-1) does not carry
TeX Live's `bibtex` package, which holds the standard styles plain, alpha,
abbrv and unsrt: the bundle packs the packages that compiled documents read,
and bibtex's reads were never recorded. Until a bundle carries it, a project
in bundle mode needs its .bst beside it, or a style from a package the bundle
has (natbib's, amscls's, ...).
